      "dom_id": "question-138314",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "The time $X,$ in weeks, between two grandkids visiting their grandma can be modeled as an exponential random variable $X∼\\text{Exp}(7).$ If a grandkid has just visited their grandma, what is the average time until the next grandkid visits their grandma?",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that if $X∼\\text{Exp}(\\lambda )$ is an exponential random variable, then\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]=\\frac{1}{\\lambda }.\n$$\n\nWe're given that $X∼\\text{Exp}(7).$ Therefore, $\\lambda =7,$ which means that grandkids visit their grandma at an average rate of $7$ visits per week. Hence,\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]=\\frac{1}{7}\\,\\text{week}=1\\,\\text{day}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the average time until the next grandkid's visit is $1$ day.",
