      "problem": "The time $X,$ in days, between two doses of medication in a patient's treatment can be modeled as an exponential random variable $X∼\\text{Exp}(6).$ If a dose has just been taken by the patient, what is the average time until the next dose?",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that if $X∼\\text{Exp}(\\lambda )$ is an exponential random variable, then\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]=\\frac{1}{\\lambda }.\n$$\n\nWe're given that $X∼\\text{Exp}(6).$ Therefore, $\\lambda =6,$ which means that $6$ doses are taken each day. Hence,\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]=\\frac{1}{6}\\,\\text{day}=4\\,\\text{h}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the average time until the next dose is $4$ hours.",
